# Line endings, pinned for the same reason the private repository pins them:
# a content fingerprint is taken over the raw bytes of these files to decide
# whether this repository is behind the source a release was built from
# (`deploy/publish-detector.ps1`, in the private repository, reusing the same
# digest `server/detector_build.py::_fingerprint` uses to decide whether the
# binary needs rebuilding). Both therefore answer to CRLF.
#
# `text eol=lf` overrides `core.autocrlf` per file, so a checkout on Windows —
# this one included — keeps LF in the working tree instead of writing back
# CRLF that would move the digest with nobody having edited a line. Without
# this file, a future `git clone` or `git reset --hard` into this checkout
# would silently disagree with the private repository over bytes nobody
# changed.
*.py text eol=lf
requirements-detector.txt text eol=lf
